From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:08:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compile the common subplan optimizer's assert-only check only when asserts are on

Assert-only code in common_subplan_optimizer.cpp binds values that only D_ASSERT()
reads, so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the
bindings are unused and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable
say so. The assert-only lines are compiled only when assertions are
enabled, with the side-effecting call kept in both builds, which is the
shape upstream gives the file later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp
index 417dbefdcf..fe541c1c1a 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/optimizer/common_subplan_optimizer.cpp
@@ -909,8 +909,12 @@ public:
 				D_ASSERT(subplan.canonical_bindings.size() == new_bindings.size());
 				for (idx_t i = 0; i < old_bindings[subplan_idx].size(); i++) {
 					replacer.replacement_bindings.emplace_back(old_bindings[subplan_idx][i], new_bindings[i]);
+#ifdef D_ASSERT_IS_ENABLED
 					const auto inserted = generated_binding_map.emplace(new_bindings[i], subplan.canonical_bindings[i]);
 					D_ASSERT(inserted.second);
+#else
+					generated_binding_map.emplace(new_bindings[i], subplan.canonical_bindings[i]);
+#endif
 				}
 			}
 
